avatar-local
============
Wraps (does not modify):
  SadTalker — https://github.com/OpenTalker/SadTalker — Apache-2.0 (third-party components listed in its LICENSE), vendored at setup time into vendor/
  Speech audio comes only from the separate tts-local tool (MeloTTS, MIT) over HTTP; no voice cloning and no TTS model is bundled.
  diffusers — https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers — Apache-2.0; models (downloaded on first use, not redistributed):
    Qwen/Qwen-Image-2512 — https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen-Image-2512 — Apache-2.0 (character pictures)
    Wan-AI/Wan2.2-I2V-A14B-Diffusers — https://huggingface.co/Wan-AI/Wan2.2-I2V-A14B-Diffusers — Apache-2.0 (picture → motion video)
  Wan2.2 — https://github.com/Wan-Video/Wan2.2 — Apache-2.0, official inference code fetched at setup time into vendor/Wan2.2 (not modified),
    runs Wan-AI/Wan2.2-S2V-14B — https://huggingface.co/Wan-AI/Wan2.2-S2V-14B — Apache-2.0 (speech → talking video, default "best quality")
  SadTalker is kept as the "fast" talking mode.
  face_alignment (BSD-3), facexlib (MIT, weights for detection/parsing), torch/torchvision (BSD)
shim/gfpgan is a local stub so SadTalker imports without gfpgan/basicsr; no GFPGAN code is used.
Files authored here (MIT): app.py studio_worker.py gpu_pick.py ui.html selftest.py setup.sh pack.sh README.md
Usage rule: only your own or explicitly consented face; no face swap and no voice cloning is implemented.

LLM (not bundled): called via an OpenAI-compatible API; default deployment is Ollama (https://github.com/ollama/ollama, MIT)
  serving Google Gemma (gemma4:31b, https://ai.google.dev/gemma — see Gemma's terms of use).

